--- !u!114 &1400437747
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1400437745}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2be8e826a6e6967499f8426bed7dc9c2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DarkFantasy.LoreNpc
  speaker: Oswin the Unreflected
  pages:
  - Don't look for my reflection in the puddle, stranger. It's not there. It hasn't
    been for forty years.
  - This was Caer Vaelmoor once. Aldric was a good king, before the Ashen crown.
    His queen Ysolde brought a mirror from the glass-temples beyond the ravine. A
    wedding gift, they said.
  - It shows you what you lack. Ysolde lacked nothing, so it showed her only herself,
    and she loved it. When the fever took her, the King stood before it day and night,
    and it showed him an empty chair.
  - 'The Mirror offered a bargain: give it reflections, and it would give her back.
    Piece by piece. The prisoners went first. I was the last one before the gaolers
    stopped bringing anyone down.'
  - The dead don't rest here because the Mirror keeps their echoes. Break it and
    every stolen reflection goes home. Mine too, maybe.
  - 'The wyrm on the terrace? Vaelthrax was Ysolde''s guardian. It still waits for
    her. Kill it and the bridge behind it lowers: that way lies the Thornwood, where
    the trees grew from the shards the Mirror spat out.'
  - One more thing. The Ossuary's western wall. Walk into it. Some walls in this
    castle are only remembering that they were walls.
  promptVerb: Talk to
  interactDistance: 5.6
  flourish: 3
  lookRoot: {fileID: 0}
