--- !u!114 &1740193495
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1740193493}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2be8e826a6e6967499f8426bed7dc9c2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DarkFantasy.LoreNpc
  speaker: The Last Minstrel
  pages:
  - Oh! A living ear. Forgive me, I have played to these stones for ninety winters
    and they never once applauded.
  - I was the Queen's own minstrel. When Ysolde died, Aldric hung her mirror in the
    throne hall and asked it to show her to him. It showed him only what he lacked.
  - 'So he fed it. A reflection here, a reflection there. Prisoners first: who would
    miss the face of a thief? Then the guards. Then the court. Then me.'
  - Without a reflection a man forgets his own face, then his name, then why he should
    stay dead. You have met the gaolers.
  - If you find the Mirror, friend, strike when its hands rest on the stone. Glass
    is proud. It never guards its own heart.
  - 'And bards: the Mirror hates music. It cannot reflect a song.'
  promptVerb: Listen to
  interactDistance: 3.2
  flourish: 1
  lookRoot: {fileID: 0}
